module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.EffectiveCartier
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Closure.SchemeTheoreticallyDense
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# The complement of a divisor cut out by nonzerodivisors is scheme-theoretically dense

[Stacks, Tag 07ZU] (Divisors, Lemma 31.14.4) says that for an effective Cartier divisor
`D ⊆ S` the open complement `U = S \ D` is an affine morphism *and* is scheme-theoretically
dense in `S`. Its own proof of the density half reduces to the affine case `S = Spec A` with
`D` cut out by a nonzerodivisor `f`, and then observes that `A ⟶ A_f` is injective.

This file proves the density half by that route. The statement it reaches,
`isSchemeTheoreticallyDense_supportCompl_of_nonZeroDivisor` below,
takes the affine-local description as its hypothesis: around every point the centre is cut out
on an affine open by a single nonzerodivisor. That description *is* the content of
[Stacks, Tag 01WS], the affine-local characterization of an effective Cartier divisor, and it is
the one input the Stacks proof of 31.14.4 uses.

This is the hypothesis `hdense` of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpUniversal.nonempty_isTerminal_blowUp_of`, one of the four
results the reduction of [Stacks, Tag 0806] still takes on faith.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CartierComplementDense.isSchemeTheoreticallyDense_of_injective_res`:
  the reduction of scheme-theoretic density of an open `U ⊆ X` to injectivity of the restriction
  maps `Γ(X, A) ⟶ Γ(X, A ⊓ U)`, for `A` ranging over all opens of `X`. This is the only place
  the definition of `IsSchemeTheoreticallyDense` is touched, and it holds for every open.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CartierComplementDense.injective_res_of_affine_nonZeroDivisor`:
  the affine computation. On an affine open where the centre is generated by a nonzerodivisor
  `f`, the restriction `Γ(X, V) ⟶ Γ(X, V ⊓ (X \ Supp I))` is injective.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CartierComplementDense`
  `.isSchemeTheoreticallyDense_supportCompl_of_nonZeroDivisor`: the density half of
  [Stacks, Tag 07ZU] from that affine-local description.

## Implementation notes

**Density is reduced to a statement about `X` itself, with no open subscheme in it.**
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.IsSchemeTheoreticallyDense U` quantifies over the opens `V` of
`X` and asks that the kernel ideal sheaf of `(V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι` vanish, a condition on the
*restricted* scheme `V.toScheme`. Two things make the transfer cheap. The kernel is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals` of the componentwise kernels, so
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.ideal_ker_le` bounds it above with no quasi-compactness
hypothesis — only the easy half of `Scheme.Hom.ker_apply` is needed, and that half is
unconditional. And `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.toScheme_presheaf_map` is `rfl`, so a
restriction map on `V.toScheme` *is* a restriction map on `X` between the images of the opens.

**The three inequalities do the work that an equality of opens would otherwise force.**
`injective_res_of_le` says that injectivity of restriction to a *smaller* open implies it for an
intermediate one, so every step needs a `≤` and never an equality of opens with an `eqToHom` to
transport across. In particular `D(f) ≤ V ⊓ (X \ Supp I)` is used where the two sides are in
fact equal, and `(V.ι ''ᵁ A) ⊓ U ≤ V.ι ''ᵁ (A ⊓ V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U)` where they are equal too.

**The nonzerodivisor survives passing to a basic open.** The generator is given on *some*
affine open `V` around a point, and the sheaf argument needs it on an affine open contained in
the ambient `A`; `AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.exists_basicOpen_le` supplies `D(g) ≤ A` inside
`V`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.map_ideal_basicOpen` carries the generator along
as the image of `f`, and `IsLocalization.map_nonZeroDivisors_le` keeps it a nonzerodivisor —
localizing at `g` cannot create a zerodivisor out of `f`.

## What is not done, and what is not claimed

**No `@[stacks 07ZU]` attribute is attached, and none may be, for two independent reasons.**
Tag 07ZU has *two* assertions — `U ⟶ S` affine, and `U` scheme-theoretically dense — and only
the second is proved here, so the covering set is incomplete. And the statement carries a
hypothesis that Tag 07ZU does not: Tag 07ZU hypothesises
`Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor`, which is invertibility of the ideal sheaf as a
sheaf of modules, whereas the theorem below
hypothesises the affine-local nonzerodivisor description. Deriving the second from the first is
the forward direction of [Stacks, Tag 01WS], and **the repository now has it**:
`Stacks.CartierAffineLocal.exists_affineOpen_nonZeroDivisor` discharges the hypothesis, and
`Stacks.CartierAffineLocal.isSchemeTheoreticallyDense_supportCompl` is the theorem below stated
unconditionally for an effective Cartier divisor. Tag 01WS itself is proved in both
directions, with the `@[stacks 01WS]` attribute on
`Stacks.CartierAffineLocalConverse.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_iff_isRegular`. So only the first
reason survives, and it is enough: Tag 07ZU's affineness assertion is proved nowhere here.

**No `@[stacks 0806]` attribute either.** This discharges at most one of the four hypotheses
that `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpSeparatedInput.nonempty_isTerminal_blowUp_of'` still
carries. It is not conditional on [Stacks, Tag 01WS]: that tag is proved, and
`Stacks.CartierAffineLocal.isSchemeTheoreticallyDense_supportCompl` is exactly the `hdense`
hypothesis of `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpUniversal.nonempty_isTerminal_blowUp_of`
(machine-checked, since `BlowUpUniversal.supportCompl D` is an `abbrev` for `D.support.compl`).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07ZU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07ZU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0806](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0806)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CartierComplementDense

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- Restriction of sections is transitive. -/
theorem res_trans {A B C : X.Opens} (hBA : B ≤ A) (hCB : C ≤ B) (s : Γ(X, A)) :
    (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hCB).op).hom ((X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hBA).op).hom s) =
      (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hCB.trans hBA)).op).hom s := by
  rw [← RingHom.comp_apply, ← CommRingCat.hom_comp, ← X.presheaf.map_comp]
  rfl

/-- Sections that agree after restriction to `B` agree after restriction to any smaller `C`. -/
theorem res_eq_of_res_eq {A B C : X.Opens} (hBA : B ≤ A) (hCB : C ≤ B) {s t : Γ(X, A)}
    (hst : (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hBA).op).hom s = (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hBA).op).hom t) :
    (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hCB.trans hBA)).op).hom s =
      (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hCB.trans hBA)).op).hom t := by
  rw [← res_trans hBA hCB, ← res_trans hBA hCB, hst]

/-- If sections over `A` restrict injectively to a small open `B`, they restrict injectively to
any intermediate open `C`. -/
theorem injective_res_of_le {A B C : X.Opens} (hCA : C ≤ A) (hBC : B ≤ C)
    (h : Function.Injective (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hBC.trans hCA)).op).hom) :
    Function.Injective (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hCA).op).hom := fun _ _ hst =>
  h (res_eq_of_res_eq hCA hBC hst)

/-- The kernel ideal sheaf of the inclusion of an open subscheme `W ⊆ Y` vanishes as soon as
sections over every open `A` of `Y` restrict injectively to `A ⊓ W`. -/
theorem ker_ι_eq_bot_of_injective_res {Y : Scheme.{u}} (W : Y.Opens)
    (h : ∀ A : Y.Opens,
      Function.Injective (Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left : A ⊓ W ≤ A)).op).hom) :
    W.ι.ker = ⊥ := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ bot_le
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.le_def]
  intro A
  have hinj : Function.Injective (W.ι.app A.1).hom := by
    rw [Scheme.Opens.ι_app]
    refine injective_res_of_le (B := A.1 ⊓ W) _ ?_ (h A.1)
    rw [Scheme.Hom.image_preimage_eq_opensRange_inf, Scheme.Opens.opensRange_ι]
    exact (inf_comm _ _).le
  refine (Scheme.Hom.ideal_ker_le _ A).trans ?_
  intro x hx
  exact Ideal.mem_bot.mpr (hinj (by simpa using hx))

/-- **Scheme-theoretic density from injectivity of restriction.** An open subscheme `U ⊆ X` is
scheme-theoretically dense as soon as, for every open `A` of `X`, the restriction map
`Γ(X, A) ⟶ Γ(X, A ⊓ U)` is injective. -/
theorem isSchemeTheoreticallyDense_of_injective_res (U : X.Opens)
    (h : ∀ A : X.Opens,
      Function.Injective (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left : A ⊓ U ≤ A)).op).hom) :
    Scheme.Opens.IsSchemeTheoreticallyDense U := by
  intro V
  refine ⟨ker_ι_eq_bot_of_injective_res _ fun A => ?_⟩
  rw [Scheme.Opens.toScheme_presheaf_map, Quiver.Hom.unop_op,
    Scheme.Hom.opensFunctor_map_homOfLE]
  refine injective_res_of_le (B := (V.ι ''ᵁ A) ⊓ U) _ ?_ (h (V.ι ''ᵁ A))
  rintro x ⟨⟨y, hy, rfl⟩, hxU⟩
  exact ⟨y, ⟨hy, hxU⟩, rfl⟩

/-- **On an affine open where the centre is generated by a nonzerodivisor, sections restrict
injectively to the complement of the support.** The complement contains the basic open `D(f)`,
and `Γ(X, D(f))` is the localization of `Γ(X, V)` at the powers of `f`, so the restriction to
`D(f)` is already injective. -/
theorem injective_res_of_affine_nonZeroDivisor (I : X.IdealSheafData) (V : X.affineOpens)
    (f : Γ(X, V.1)) (hf : f ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, V.1))
    (hgen : I.ideal V = Ideal.span {f}) :
    Function.Injective (X.presheaf.map
      (homOfLE (inf_le_left : (V.1 : X.Opens) ⊓ I.support.compl ≤ V.1)).op).hom := by
  have hzero : X.zeroLocus (U := V.1) (I.ideal V) = (↑(X.basicOpen f))ᶜ := by
    rw [hgen, X.zeroLocus_span (U := V.1) {f}, X.zeroLocus_singleton]
  have hsub : X.basicOpen f ≤ (V.1 : X.Opens) ⊓ I.support.compl := by
    refine le_inf (X.basicOpen_le f) fun x hx => ?_
    have hxV : x ∈ V.1 := X.basicOpen_le f hx
    simp only [TopologicalSpace.Closeds.compl, Opens.mem_mk, Set.mem_compl_iff, SetLike.mem_coe]
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_support_iff_of_mem hxV, hzero]
    exact fun h => h hx
  refine injective_res_of_le _ hsub ?_
  have : IsLocalization.Away f Γ(X, X.basicOpen f) := V.2.isLocalization_basicOpen f
  have hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap Γ(X, V.1) Γ(X, X.basicOpen f)) :=
    IsLocalization.injective _ (Submonoid.powers_le.mpr hf)
  rwa [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra] at hinj

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 07ZU, from the affine-local nonzerodivisor description of the
divisor.** If the centre `I` is, around every point, cut out on an affine open by a single
nonzerodivisor, then the open complement of its support is scheme-theoretically dense. -/
@[ega "IV 20.2.9" "special case"]
theorem isSchemeTheoreticallyDense_supportCompl_of_nonZeroDivisor (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (hloc : ∀ x : X, ∃ V : X.affineOpens, x ∈ (V : Set X) ∧ ∃ f : Γ(X, V.1),
      f ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, V.1) ∧ I.ideal V = Ideal.span {f}) :
    Scheme.Opens.IsSchemeTheoreticallyDense I.support.compl := by
  refine isSchemeTheoreticallyDense_of_injective_res _ fun B s t hst => ?_
  refine X.IsSheaf.section_ext (U := Opposite.op B) fun x hxB => ?_
  obtain ⟨V, hxV, f, hf, hgen⟩ := hloc x
  obtain ⟨g, hgB, hxg⟩ := V.2.exists_basicOpen_le (⟨x, hxB⟩ : B) hxV
  refine ⟨X.basicOpen g, hgB, hxg, ?_⟩
  change (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hgB).op).hom s = (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hgB).op).hom t
  -- The ideal on `D(g)` is generated by the image of `f`, still a nonzerodivisor.
  have hres : IsLocalization.Away g Γ(X, X.basicOpen g) := V.2.isLocalization_basicOpen g
  have hfW : (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op).hom f ∈
      nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, X.basicOpen g) := by
    refine IsLocalization.map_nonZeroDivisors_le (M := Submonoid.powers g)
      (S := Γ(X, X.basicOpen g)) ?_
    rw [← RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op).hom]
    exact ⟨f, hf, rfl⟩
  have hgenW : I.ideal (X.affineBasicOpen g) = Ideal.span
      {(X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op).hom f} := by
    rw [← I.map_ideal_basicOpen V g, hgen, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]
  have hinj : Function.Injective (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left :
      (X.basicOpen g : X.Opens) ⊓ I.support.compl ≤ X.basicOpen g)).op).hom :=
    injective_res_of_affine_nonZeroDivisor I (X.affineBasicOpen g) _ hfW hgenW
  refine hinj ?_
  -- Both restrictions to `D(g) ⊓ Uᶜ` come from the common restriction to `B ⊓ Uᶜ`.
  rw [res_trans hgB inf_le_left s, res_trans hgB inf_le_left t]
  exact res_eq_of_res_eq inf_le_left (inf_le_inf_right (I.support.compl) hgB) hst

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CartierComplementDense

end
